# cloud-copilot phone push configuration (ntfy).
#
# Copy this file to  ~/.config/cloud-copilot/notify.env  and fill in real values.
# Every value can also be supplied as a plain environment variable, which wins
# over this file. Leave NTFY_TOPIC empty (or delete the file) to turn pushes off
# entirely — nothing is sent and nothing errors.
#
# The server sends ONE push per finished job, naming the repo, the action and
# the issue/PR number or chat title, e.g.
#   ✅ Create PR · cloud-copilot#27   /   ❌ Deploy · ios-diet-expert PR #112 失败
# The old generic "[repo] session complete" hook is silenced automatically for
# jobs started by cloud-copilot (they run with CLOUD_COPILOT_JOB=1).

# --- Where to publish ---
# Your ntfy topic IS the credential: anyone who knows it can read your pushes.
# Pick something long and unguessable, and subscribe to it in the ntfy app.
NTFY_TOPIC=
# Self-hosted ntfy? Point this at it. Defaults to the public server.
NTFY_SERVER=https://ntfy.sh
# Only needed for protected topics / self-hosted instances with auth.
NTFY_TOKEN=

# --- Behaviour ---
# Set to 0 to keep the config but stop sending.
NTFY_ENABLED=1

# --- Deep links ---
# Base URL of THIS cloud-copilot instance as reachable from your phone (LAN IP,
# tailnet name, or tunnel). Used for the notification's tap target, e.g.
# http://192.168.1.20:8787 → .../#/pr/<repo>/<issue>/<pr>. Leave empty to send
# pushes without a tap-through link.
APP_BASE_URL=
